{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 5368eca0, for S4: the release is at the Agent's\nhandoff, as you recommend.\n\n1. The Agent releases the private candidate when it returns the code to\n   the trusted Registry. The Registry then makes its final membership\n   judgment and settles its own rows.\n2. The Registry promises no validity of the candidate at delivery and\n   holds no lease on it. Another allowed Agent operation can consume\n   the code or change the private config before the Registry relays\n   its result. The contract says so in those words.\n3. Every use of the credential gets fresh admission. That check, not\n   the relay, is what keeps a consumed or revoked credential from\n   working.\n4. No remote candidate protocol. A second read of the Agent followed by\n   another await cannot lock both objects, so it would add calls and\n   prove nothing more.\n5. Witness: a relay whose code another operation consumed first is\n   delivered, and its use is refused by the fresh admission.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}